      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Edit: This happens reliably if whatever you're using for \"SIL\" is set to a null value (no vertex actually moves on sil), or you don't have a blend-shape properly associated with silent.\nThere's a very, (very) brief moment as well where when you change avatars, while your mic is open, where you'll hear yourself for a blip, even if it doesn't persist after you're back in. This is because the audio is tied to your avatar location (and the mesh, not the parent gameobject with your nameplate) and it has to do with the fact that directional audio orientation is tied to your head on your avatar: so loading an avatar creates a new game-object to do that calculation: essentially the sound isn't coming \"from you\" anymore, so you hear yourself. \nI could see that occasionally becoming desynced, as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
